From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pbs05 <27010143+pbs05@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] system-linux: report device type without link settings

system_if_dump_info() returns early when a network device does not support
ETHTOOL_GLINKSETTINGS. This leaves the devtype attribute out of the ubus
device status for virtual devices such as 802.1Q VLAN interfaces.

firewall4 uses devtype to resolve VLAN and bridge interfaces to their lower
devices when building a hardware flowtable. A VLAN without devtype remains
in the flowtable device set while its physical lower device is omitted.

Report devtype before querying link settings because the device topology is
independent of ethtool link mode support.

Signed-off-by: pbs05 <27010143+pbs05@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 system-linux.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/system-linux.c
+++ b/system-linux.c
@@ -3520,6 +3520,11 @@ system_if_dump_info(struct device *dev,
 	void *c, *d;
 	char *s;
 
+	/* Device topology is available for virtual interfaces which do not
+	 * implement ETHTOOL_GLINKSETTINGS. Keep devtype independent of the
+	 * optional link-mode query below.
+	 */
+	system_add_devtype(b, dev->ifname);
 	system_get_ethtool_pause(dev, &rx_pause, &tx_pause, &pause_autoneg);
 
 	memset(&ecmd, 0, sizeof(ecmd));
@@ -3599,8 +3604,6 @@ system_if_dump_info(struct device *dev,
 	blobmsg_add_u8(b, "hw-tc-offload",
 		ethtool_feature_value(dev->ifname, "hw-tc-offload"));
 
-	system_add_devtype(b, dev->ifname);
-
 	/* Add PSE (PoE) status if available */
 	{
 		struct pse_reply_data pse_data;
-- 
